No owner or developer shall perform any land development activities without first meeting the requirements of this chapter prior to commencing the proposed activity. Unless specifically exempted by this chapter, any owner or developer proposing a land development activity shall submit to the city a permit application on a form provided by the planning and zoning administrator for that purpose.
Unless otherwise exempted by this chapter, the following items shall accompany a permit application in order to be considered:
(1) Stormwater concept plan and consultation meeting certification in accordance with section 107-52;
(2) Stormwater management plan in accordance with section 107-53;
(3) Inspection and maintenance agreement and covenant in accordance with section 107-54, if applicable;
(4) Performance bond in accordance with section 107-55 and the city's utility dedication ordinance; and
(5) Permit application and plan review fees in accordance with section 2-110.
(Ord. of 2-6-2006, § 3.1; Ord. of 8-19-2019, § 13)
